WEBVTT

00:00:00.940 --> 00:00:03.610
In the stormy Pantasia newcomers’ battle,

00:00:03.610 --> 00:00:07.400
Azuma Kazuma and Kawachi Kyousuke were representing the Southern Tokyo branch.

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:09.400
They had triumphed over the themes of
dinner bread, from the first preliminaries,

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:12.570
and the butter roll, from the second preliminaries.

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:16.670
They then faced the theme of the
first round of the finals – melon bread.

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:22.160
The opponent Azuma had to face was
Tsukino’s little sister, Azusagawa Mizuno.

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:27.670
She took up the challenge by using the
highest grade muskmelon in her melon bread.

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:29.670
Azuma, who opposed her, made...

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:33.300
<i>Japan</i> #58. Melon sushi bread!

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:37.340
O-Oh, no!

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:39.980
I guess it came, after all!

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:43.480
MELON!!

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:47.520
Victor: Azuma Kazuma!

00:00:48.110 --> 00:00:51.450
It’s a promise.
Address Tsukino as “nee-chan.”

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:54.490
I’ll have my Koala-chan take my revenge for me,

00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:56.540
so until then, the promise is on hold!

00:00:57.030 --> 00:00:58.080
Hey!

00:00:58.080 --> 00:00:59.910
Don’t go changing the promise like that!

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:01.120
It’s all right, Azuma-san.

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:04.380
It’s settled with you not having to go anywhere.

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:05.920
Just that is enough.

00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:12.340
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:14.260
but Japan´s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:16.550
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:19.930
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:25.190
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:28.910
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:46.080
Somewhere far away, there are people listening carefully.

00:01:47.410 --> 00:01:54.050
In every place, there are people looking up at the sky.

00:01:55.170 --> 00:02:01.930
Under the night sky, we, who are whistling...

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:09.640
without words, are just tracing constellations with our fingers.

00:02:09.890 --> 00:02:17.110
The dreams of the cold-sensitive... Your cold hands...

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:26.500
The warming magic is to believe in one path.

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:35.250
The single star found on the other side of the comet cloud...

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:39.510
whether it be a shining or a faint star...

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:42.510
is the light of only you.

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:46.250
On the other side of the cloud in your heart,

00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:51.060
is a sign post that remains unseen.

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:58.780
Now, opening these hands, what will you believe in today?

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:02.740
Delii-cious!!

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:05.090
The trap of the yakisoba bread!

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:11.500
Azusagawa Mizuno
Azuma Kazuma

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:19.720
Kawachi, are things all right
over at your end?

00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:22.680
Melon bread’s a specialty of mine.

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:27.600
Moreover, I now have these Solar Gauntlets.
I’m invincible.

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:33.230
The Solar Gauntlets are not a tool
to satisfy your self-conceit, Kawachi!

00:03:34.030 --> 00:03:36.730
Kawachi, see that lady over there?

00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:39.070
Huh? Oh yeah...

00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:40.740
Her name’s Motohashi Yuuko.

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:41.530
Kawachi Kyousuke
Motohashi Yuuko

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:42.990
She’s your opponent.
Kawachi Kyousuke
Motohashi Yuuko

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:45.750
Really? That’s a real let down.

00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:47.660
An old lady like that as my opponent is...

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:48.920
Don’t underestimate her!

00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:50.960
You can’t judge people
by their appearances.

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:53.960
She has reigned over the
school lunch industry for 30 years.

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:57.050
She’s the Top Queen of the School Lunch Center.

00:03:57.050 --> 00:03:59.090
Possessor of “Mother’s Hands,”

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:00.590
Motohashi Yuuko!

00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:02.140
What?!

00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:03.560
Mother’s Hands?!

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:04.510
What in the world...?

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:15.860
Little boy, I’m sorry, but I’m getting a running start from the very beginning.

00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:20.860
W-Wrist weights!

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:33.260
How can wrist weights be so heavy?!

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:46.720
It’s as though the whole Earth’s trembling...

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:54.650
M-O-TH-ER HA!!!

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:02.690
The fearsome Mother’s Hands..

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:07.200
To think this old woman
possessed these miracle hands...

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:09.620
A formidable enemy in the very first round...

00:05:09.620 --> 00:05:11.540
Can I win?

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:14.580
Everyone is at their places, right?

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:19.290
Then, the B group may begin their
work for the first round of the finals!

00:05:28.850 --> 00:05:30.270
What can I do...?

00:05:33.230 --> 00:05:37.030
What can I do to win?!

00:05:38.650 --> 00:05:41.660
Victor: Kawachi Kyousuke!

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:43.690
Eh?

00:05:43.690 --> 00:05:44.860
Yes!

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:45.620
We did it!

00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:47.660
Good going, Kawachi!

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:51.040
Using crunchy pie dough instead of cookie dough,

00:05:51.040 --> 00:05:53.300
and mixing it in with the bread dough...

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:56.830
It was a wonderful melon bread.

00:05:57.710 --> 00:05:59.390
It’s a complete victory for you.

00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:03.470
Eh...? Eh...? Eh...?

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:08.890
Aww... I guess I really can’t
match up to someone young.

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:14.900
At this age, I had suddenly decided
to change my occupation to a baker,

00:06:15.190 --> 00:06:17.390
but it’s really hard, isn’t it?

00:06:17.650 --> 00:06:21.860
But you know, since at least I
got to the finals, I have no regrets.

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:23.650
Thank you very much, little boy.

00:06:24.700 --> 00:06:26.200
Hang on, ma’am.

00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:28.860
You’re not the Top Queen of the School Lunch Center?

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:30.130
Huh?!

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:32.330
Ma’am!

00:06:32.330 --> 00:06:34.800
Don’t you use the Mother’s Hands?

00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:36.670
A Mother’s Hands?

00:06:36.670 --> 00:06:40.300
I definitely have 3 children,

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:42.600
but what relation does that bear to anything?

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:53.400
You’re really a funny kid...

00:06:55.890 --> 00:06:57.990
Continue working hard in the next round as well, okay?

00:07:01.270 --> 00:07:02.480
Hold on a second!

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:05.190
Saying that she was the
school lunch industry’s Top Queen,

00:07:05.190 --> 00:07:08.570
and having Mother’s Hands or something...
Scaring me with crazy stuff like that...

00:07:08.570 --> 00:07:09.490
What are you thinking?!

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:12.920
Hey!!

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:14.620
Are you making fun of me?!

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:15.200
Calm down, Kawachi!
Are you making fun of me?!

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:16.660
Please calm down, Kawachi-san!
Calm down, Kawachi!

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:21.040
Desperately, with great trouble, I used pie
dough instead of cookie dough in my bread!

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:25.010
I made my Super Sunrise Crush Melon Bread, and...

00:07:25.010 --> 00:07:26.670
There’s nothing special about that!!

00:07:27.050 --> 00:07:28.710
W-What?!

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:31.380
Letting your guard down is your worst enemy.

00:07:31.380 --> 00:07:33.260
Blood had gone to your head.

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:34.760
Huh?

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:37.940
You definitely may have matured a little.

00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:40.940
But just because you’ve attained the Solar Gauntlets,

00:07:40.940 --> 00:07:43.150
or because your opponent was an old lady...

00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:45.280
you had clearly let your guard down.

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:49.200
Competing with such an attitude,

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:52.470
you can’t win against the
stronger enemies to come from now on.

00:07:52.470 --> 00:07:53.320
Am I wrong?

00:07:55.370 --> 00:07:57.280
It’s mortifying, but it’s true...

00:07:58.160 --> 00:08:00.710
At that time, I had let my guard down.

00:08:00.710 --> 00:08:03.220
Manager, what’s so funny?

00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:05.380
I’m really sorry.

00:08:05.380 --> 00:08:08.260
Thank you for watching out for me, Manager...

00:08:08.260 --> 00:08:11.170
Not at all... it’s okay if you understand...

00:08:11.890 --> 00:08:12.850
Oh, well...

00:08:12.850 --> 00:08:14.890
Yoohoo... How are you all doing?

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:18.770
Tsukino-oneesan.

00:08:20.190 --> 00:08:21.390
Mizuno...

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:23.390
Mizuno!

00:08:23.390 --> 00:08:26.360
Hold on, don’t misunderstand anything here.

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:28.400
It’s just that I kept my promise, that’s all.

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:30.400
Once I thought it over...

00:08:30.910 --> 00:08:34.450
Being-stubborn over not calling you “oneesan” is...

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:36.360
Well, it’s no big deal, after all...

00:08:36.790 --> 00:08:40.580
No matter how much you hate that person...

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:43.410
How dare you!! I can’t forgive that!

00:08:43.410 --> 00:08:44.870
Oh, no! I can’t stop!

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:46.920
He’s a moron.

00:08:47.340 --> 00:08:49.310
So, what is it that you want?

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:51.420
If we go in order,

00:08:51.970 --> 00:08:56.180
then our Koala-chan and Kazu-kun will be
challenging each other in the third round.

00:08:56.180 --> 00:08:57.140
Over there...

00:08:57.140 --> 00:08:59.060
Based on that result,

00:08:59.060 --> 00:09:01.690
how about either Tsukino-oneesan or me stepping down

00:09:01.690 --> 00:09:05.560
from the battle over the
succession of the Pantasia group?

00:09:06.020 --> 00:09:07.150
Don’t be talking nonsense!

00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:08.480
We understand!

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:09.900
Even if that koala loses,

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:12.240
you probably plan to run off on us like before.

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:14.900
Like we could trust a spoiled brat like you...

00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:16.990
I thought you’d say that...

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:19.410
Here, take a look at this!
A written contract!

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:22.000
If necessary,

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:25.750
it’ll be fine to have you guys
keep this until the challenge is over.

00:09:25.750 --> 00:09:26.880
However...

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:28.290
I’ll have Tsukino-oneesan
properly sign the same thing as well.

00:09:28.290 --> 00:09:31.130
Written Contract

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:34.130
Fine, then.

00:09:37.890 --> 00:09:39.140
Azusagawa Tsukino

00:09:39.390 --> 00:09:40.270
Okay!

00:09:40.270 --> 00:09:41.680
So, were all decided, aren’t we?

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:43.690
I think you know this,

00:09:43.690 --> 00:09:46.860
but if Kazu-kun loses before fighting with Koala-chan,

00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:48.730
then that counts as your loss, okay?

00:09:49.280 --> 00:09:51.360
That’s our line!

00:09:51.360 --> 00:09:53.490
If that koala is to lose in the second round,

00:09:53.490 --> 00:09:55.870
then it’s automatically your loss, okay, idiot?

00:09:55.870 --> 00:09:56.740
Exactly!

00:09:57.780 --> 00:09:59.670
Koala-chan, lose?

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:09.080
Is this really okay, Tsukino?

00:10:10.590 --> 00:10:15.300
Yes. Becoming the successor isn’t everything to me.

00:10:15.720 --> 00:10:18.720
Of course, I have my pride, but...

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:21.430
Right now, I have Azuma-san,

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:24.110
Kawachi-san, and Manager.

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:27.020
I have such a charming store...

00:10:27.440 --> 00:10:31.020
I’m really happy with just that.

00:10:35.730 --> 00:10:39.700
Just now, I felt really alienated.

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:40.740
I wonder why...

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:43.700
Anyway, we just have to win.

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:44.240
Yeah!

00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:45.700
Fight!

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:47.170
Yeah!

00:10:47.170 --> 00:10:49.170
I hope it goes well...

00:10:49.170 --> 00:10:51.250
Oh, no!

00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:54.260
The Drasans have lost, huh?

00:10:54.260 --> 00:10:56.760
Nikkuki Tigers, what are you going to do about this?

00:10:57.050 --> 00:10:57.970
What?

00:10:57.970 --> 00:11:02.140
There’s some weird foreigner
speaking fluent Japanese mixed in among us.

00:11:02.140 --> 00:11:04.350
Huh? Kansai dialect?

00:11:04.350 --> 00:11:08.560
Hey, you! Seeing that you speak a Kansai
dialect, I’m guessing that you’re from Kansai?

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:09.980
If so, what about it?

00:11:10.310 --> 00:11:11.520
An enemy!

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:12.480
Why?

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:14.990
No why’s or but’s.

00:11:15.490 --> 00:11:17.160
Azuma.

00:11:18.240 --> 00:11:21.410
I saw that you had an excellent first round.

00:11:21.410 --> 00:11:22.700
Who are you?

00:11:22.700 --> 00:11:25.080
Oh, sorry for the delay in introductions.

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:29.750
I’m the representative from Nagoya prefecture, Spencer Henley Hokou.

00:11:29.750 --> 00:11:33.250
You can shorten it and lovingly call me Shachihoko!

00:11:33.250 --> 00:11:34.750
Shachihoko?

00:11:35.460 --> 00:11:37.430
Spencer Henley Hokou,

00:11:37.430 --> 00:11:39.050
shortened to Shachihoko.

00:11:39.050 --> 00:11:40.760
He’s your next opponent.

00:11:42.810 --> 00:11:44.680
Oh, that’s true.

00:11:44.680 --> 00:11:45.470
Best regards.

00:11:45.980 --> 00:11:47.640
Me, too! Bang!

00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:49.810
How could you possibly be from Nagoya prefecture?

00:11:49.810 --> 00:11:51.270
There’s no such prefecture.

00:11:51.270 --> 00:11:53.190
Japan may say anything it likes,

00:11:53.190 --> 00:11:56.230
but I’m a true citizen of Nagoya prefecture.

00:11:56.230 --> 00:11:57.490
You dumbass!

00:11:57.490 --> 00:11:59.570
That’s why I’m trying to tell you, there’s no such thing!

00:11:59.570 --> 00:12:00.990
Hey, there!

00:12:00.990 --> 00:12:04.330
Can you not feel this Nagoya spirit here?

00:12:04.330 --> 00:12:06.780
I’m the #1 citizen of Nagoya prefecture!

00:12:06.780 --> 00:12:09.540
Moreover, are you even a Japanese citizen?

00:12:09.540 --> 00:12:12.590
If you’re a Japanese citizen, then you shouldn’t be dyeing your hair blond now, should you?

00:12:12.590 --> 00:12:14.300
So, get a little level-headed, will ya?

00:12:15.250 --> 00:12:17.720
This is... this is tiring.

00:12:19.090 --> 00:12:22.390
But with a fellow like this, it’s an easy win, right?

00:12:22.390 --> 00:12:24.800
Kick him in my place, Azuma.

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:29.280
And then, that reputed Koala fellow, too.

00:12:33.860 --> 00:12:35.780
Kawachi, doesn’t that hurt?

00:12:36.980 --> 00:12:38.770
Spencer Henley Hokou,

00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:40.900
who was trained in Italy

00:12:40.900 --> 00:12:44.280
and is the American California state bread guild examination champion.

00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:47.750
I tried to scout him for the New Tokyo Branch,

00:12:47.750 --> 00:12:49.870
but he has a real Nagoya fetish,

00:12:49.870 --> 00:12:51.750
so he turned down my invitation.

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:53.540
A self-styled Nagoya prefecture citizen.

00:12:55.840 --> 00:12:57.170
Kazu-kun...

00:12:57.170 --> 00:13:02.010
you probably won’t even be able to make
it to the third round to fight Koala-chan.

00:13:10.730 --> 00:13:14.520
Those who have passed the first
round are to gather at Assembly Hall #4.

00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:15.610
I repeat,

00:13:15.610 --> 00:13:18.780
those who have passed the first round
of the Pantasia newcomers’ battle finals,

00:13:18.780 --> 00:13:21.020
gather at Assembly Hall #4.

00:13:26.870 --> 00:13:29.910
Well then, I will announce
the theme for the second round.

00:13:29.910 --> 00:13:31.130
It’s yakisoba!

00:13:31.130 --> 00:13:31.980
Note: “Yakisoba” is fried buckwheat noodles.

00:13:32.750 --> 00:13:36.290
When you say yakisoba,
do you mean yakisoba bread?

00:13:36.880 --> 00:13:37.960
Yes.

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:41.290
However, this time, you don’t have to make the bread.

00:13:43.300 --> 00:13:45.300
We have prepared the bread,

00:13:45.300 --> 00:13:47.220
and we’ll have you use these French rolls.

00:13:47.220 --> 00:13:50.690
You people have to make the
yakisoba that goes with this bread.

00:13:51.680 --> 00:13:52.690
Moreover, this time,

00:13:52.690 --> 00:13:56.190
we plan to choose the best
yakisoba bread from amongst the winners,

00:13:56.190 --> 00:13:58.730
and present them with a reward of 100,000 yen!

00:14:00.480 --> 00:14:02.730
Wow! That’s really generous!

00:14:02.730 --> 00:14:05.030
Furthermore, in reverse order from the first round,

00:14:05.030 --> 00:14:07.620
the competition, to be held the day
after tomorrow, will start with the B group,

00:14:07.620 --> 00:14:09.530
with the A group proceeding on the day after that.

00:14:09.530 --> 00:14:11.540
Good luck to all of you.

00:14:11.540 --> 00:14:13.210
That’s all. Disperse.

00:14:23.720 --> 00:14:25.930
This time, it seems to be kinda fun...

00:14:25.930 --> 00:14:27.850
There’s a reward, too.

00:14:27.850 --> 00:14:29.760
But why is it yakisoba bread?

00:14:30.240 --> 00:14:34.190
Originally, Pantasia had never
considered becoming a chain.

00:14:34.690 --> 00:14:36.730
If was a small store, managed personally by the owner,

00:14:36.730 --> 00:14:41.200
Azusagawa Sadano,
with just eight people.

00:14:42.360 --> 00:14:44.740
However, it earned a really high reputation,

00:14:44.740 --> 00:14:48.280
and began to increase its tempo,
later expanding into a chain.

00:14:48.280 --> 00:14:51.240
The Pantasia enterprise was
established and rose to its present status,

00:14:51.240 --> 00:14:55.710
but until now, it’s been an
over-the-counter sales store.

00:14:56.170 --> 00:14:59.290
The lines of school and college
lunches are still not up to par.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:00.880
From now on,

00:15:00.880 --> 00:15:03.420
they are considering adding
convenience store products to their stores.

00:15:03.420 --> 00:15:06.930
They plan to increase marketing of products
other than those available over the counter.

00:15:07.390 --> 00:15:09.430
The butter rolls from the preliminaries is an example.

00:15:09.430 --> 00:15:11.440
The same goes for this round’s yakisoba bread.

00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:13.810
They must plan to come up with new products from

00:15:13.810 --> 00:15:18.270
the accomplishments of you young
newcomers, and thus meet their target.

00:15:18.850 --> 00:15:20.820
I see.

00:15:25.150 --> 00:15:30.450
Hey! Azuma. What’s wrong with you?
You don’t seem to be very energetic.

00:15:31.870 --> 00:15:32.950
I’ve...

00:15:33.490 --> 00:15:36.420
never made it... yakisoba...

00:15:37.580 --> 00:15:41.960
You talk about <i>Japan</i>,
but you’ve never made a yakisoba bread?

00:15:41.960 --> 00:15:45.010
I’ve made yakisoba bread,

00:15:45.460 --> 00:15:49.430
but the yakisoba for the filling
was always made by my sister.

00:15:49.430 --> 00:15:52.470
I’ve never made anything but the bread.

00:15:53.260 --> 00:15:55.220
You’ve really never made it?

00:15:55.220 --> 00:15:56.180
Nope.

00:15:56.890 --> 00:16:02.110
Come to think of it... I’ve never really
seen him cook regular food...

00:16:02.480 --> 00:16:06.690
At most, I’ve only seen him make sauce
for flavoring bread... and butter.

00:16:07.030 --> 00:16:08.440
No way...

00:16:09.150 --> 00:16:11.370
Then, it’s pretty much like we’ve lost...

00:16:11.370 --> 00:16:12.830
Don’t tell me that all possibility of my becoming

00:16:12.830 --> 00:16:15.880
the successor is going to
disappear because of an idiot like you...

00:16:20.460 --> 00:16:21.790
You dullard.

00:16:21.790 --> 00:16:23.970
Manager, what is it that you’re doing...?

00:16:24.550 --> 00:16:28.050
Oh, nothing. I just thought to act
as a proxy for Tsukino’s inner voice.

00:16:28.050 --> 00:16:29.960
I’m thinking no such thing!

00:16:30.180 --> 00:16:31.470
What’s this!

00:16:31.470 --> 00:16:33.550
We can’t afford to lose!

00:16:33.550 --> 00:16:37.060
Let’s start by selecting your noodles.
I’ll introduce you to someone amazing!

00:16:37.060 --> 00:16:39.060
You can just learn to make it over there, too.

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:40.730
So, everyone follow me!

00:16:40.730 --> 00:16:42.320
Let’s go!

00:16:43.560 --> 00:16:45.560
Ah, he ran off...

00:16:48.570 --> 00:16:51.570
Chinese noodles wholesale retail
Ryuusei Noodles

00:16:56.990 --> 00:16:59.080
Yo. Ryuu-san, it’s been a while.

00:17:16.350 --> 00:17:19.270
Oh! It’s Ken. Ken, you been well?

00:17:19.270 --> 00:17:21.220
Ryuu-san, you too. Glad to see you’re well.

00:17:23.150 --> 00:17:25.560
Very nostalgic. How long it been?

00:17:25.560 --> 00:17:29.690
It’s been since we annihilated Ya-san’s group
for messing with us at the coaching classes...

00:17:29.690 --> 00:17:31.230
so it must be about 3 years...

00:17:32.180 --> 00:17:33.520
Oh, that’s right.

00:17:33.520 --> 00:17:35.640
We may have gone a little overboard that time, right?

00:17:35.640 --> 00:17:36.740
I’ve reflected upon it.

00:17:37.980 --> 00:17:40.820
But at that time, Ken was really scary.

00:17:40.820 --> 00:17:42.360
You did about 50, right?

00:17:42.360 --> 00:17:43.490
Can you really say anything?

00:17:43.490 --> 00:17:46.750
I mean, you nearly killed about 70, didn’t you?

00:17:47.110 --> 00:17:49.620
I... remembered something important...

00:17:51.620 --> 00:17:53.210
These are young employees of ours.

00:17:53.910 --> 00:17:56.000
Hey! Greet him.

00:17:56.000 --> 00:17:57.720
Ah! They bow heads well.

00:17:58.290 --> 00:17:59.960
This here is Ryuu Ryomen-san.

00:17:59.960 --> 00:18:01.550
He’s an expert at noodle-making,

00:18:01.550 --> 00:18:05.840
and is the successor of the ancient Chinese assassination group, Ryuuke Shinken.

00:18:05.840 --> 00:18:08.640
We got to know each other a
long time back, in a faraway place...

00:18:09.720 --> 00:18:12.730
Nothing but a really bad image comes to mind.

00:18:13.600 --> 00:18:14.810
So, Ryuu-san...

00:18:14.810 --> 00:18:16.740
as you may have guessed, we’ve come here today for...

00:18:17.350 --> 00:18:18.990
Don’t be so distant, Ken.

00:18:19.270 --> 00:18:20.900
If it’s a request from Ken, then...

00:18:20.900 --> 00:18:22.230
I’ll take on anything.

00:18:22.230 --> 00:18:24.740
So, who is it I have to kill?

00:18:25.110 --> 00:18:26.530
No, I don’t need an assassination.

00:18:26.530 --> 00:18:28.830
I just need you to teach them something...

00:18:30.070 --> 00:18:32.870
Okay! So, it starts from the stance,

00:18:32.870 --> 00:18:35.910
in order to send your opponent to the
other world in one blow, then sengetsu.

00:18:35.910 --> 00:18:38.500
Make a pose like this, keep your legs apart,

00:18:38.500 --> 00:18:40.290
and lower our hips!

00:18:40.290 --> 00:18:42.540
That’s enough regarding the assassination stuff.

00:18:42.540 --> 00:18:44.000
Then, what is it?!

00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:45.020
Noodles, right? Noodles!

00:18:45.020 --> 00:18:48.560
I-I wonder if he’s all right? This person...

00:18:49.840 --> 00:18:50.800
Yes, yes... yes...

00:18:50.800 --> 00:18:53.190
You, too, don’t obey him while being so scared.
Yes, yes... yes...

00:18:53.190 --> 00:18:54.770
You, too, don’t obey him while being so scared.

00:18:55.430 --> 00:18:56.780
Yakisoba bread?

00:18:57.350 --> 00:18:59.390
If you want noodles that go with yakisoba bread,

00:18:59.390 --> 00:19:00.940
then I guess you need mushimen.
Note: Mushimen – steamed ram doodles.

00:19:00.940 --> 00:19:01.780
Mushimen?
Note: Mushimen – steamed ram doodles.

00:19:02.230 --> 00:19:05.190
Steamed noodles are less watery than they seem,

00:19:05.190 --> 00:19:07.290
and this way, taste sets in.
It go well with yakisoba bread.

00:19:09.070 --> 00:19:10.290
Good to come this way.

00:19:10.950 --> 00:19:12.280
Hot!!

00:19:12.280 --> 00:19:15.200
Hot, hot, hot, hot, hot, hot!!

00:19:15.200 --> 00:19:16.870
Hot! This is hot!

00:19:16.870 --> 00:19:17.880
It’s really hot!

00:19:19.040 --> 00:19:20.590
Amazing frying pan technique.

00:19:21.460 --> 00:19:22.580
Try it, try it.

00:19:22.580 --> 00:19:24.550
Itadakimasu!

00:19:33.010 --> 00:19:35.470
Delii-cious!!

00:19:35.470 --> 00:19:39.980
The noodles are swelled up and are completely holding the taste in. This is really good.

00:19:39.980 --> 00:19:42.730
This is the first time I’ve eaten such delicious noodles!

00:19:42.730 --> 00:19:44.190
Of course.

00:19:44.190 --> 00:19:45.690
My noodles are the best in the world.

00:19:45.690 --> 00:19:46.690
Come on, next.

00:19:46.690 --> 00:19:48.120
It’s your turn.

00:19:51.120 --> 00:19:54.130
Ah! It’s hot. It’s hot. HOT!

00:19:55.240 --> 00:19:57.660
There’s hope for the Kansai-state boy.

00:19:57.660 --> 00:20:00.340
There’s no such state,
but this is really unexpected.

00:20:00.790 --> 00:20:04.920
I had to make food everyday for my siblings,

00:20:04.920 --> 00:20:06.630
so yakisoba, curry, and croquettes...

00:20:06.630 --> 00:20:10.760
I can make all of the common people’s food.

00:20:11.380 --> 00:20:14.600
For a commoner like me,
I’d also say that this is good...

00:20:15.430 --> 00:20:16.350
Dammit...

00:20:16.350 --> 00:20:17.730
I can also...

00:20:19.060 --> 00:20:21.640
Hot! It’s Hot! It’s H-h-h-hot! It’s very hot!

00:20:21.640 --> 00:20:24.030
But the hairband kid’s not quite up to the mark, is he?
Hot! It’s Hot! It’s H-h-h-hot! It’s very hot!

00:20:24.030 --> 00:20:27.270
It’s my first time seeing such an Azuma-san.

00:20:27.270 --> 00:20:28.400
That’s really unsightly.

00:20:28.400 --> 00:20:31.150
However, should he practice here all day,

00:20:31.150 --> 00:20:34.360
even the hairband boy might improve a little.

00:20:34.360 --> 00:20:36.210
If not, he will be executed.

00:20:36.530 --> 00:20:38.800
All right! I’ll work hard!

00:20:38.800 --> 00:20:43.000
Oh well, I can relax a little with this...

00:20:43.000 --> 00:20:45.080
That Shachihoko guy’s a westerner...

00:20:45.080 --> 00:20:46.670
He may be good at baking bread,

00:20:46.670 --> 00:20:48.670
but as for making yakisoba, he must be a novice.

00:20:48.670 --> 00:20:52.890
And Nagoya residents don’t really have anything to do with yakisoba in particular anyway...

00:20:54.720 --> 00:20:57.260
A westerner who’s a resident of Nagoya.

00:20:57.260 --> 00:20:58.690
Shachihoko...

00:20:59.060 --> 00:21:00.720
S.H. Hokou...

00:21:00.720 --> 00:21:03.320
Spencer Henley Hokou...

00:21:03.320 --> 00:21:04.280
That’s...

00:21:04.900 --> 00:21:06.320
This, right?

00:21:06.320 --> 00:21:09.080
Book Title: Monthly Publication – The Noodle Experts
100 selections of delicious stuff

00:21:16.030 --> 00:21:16.880
This is...

00:21:17.450 --> 00:21:18.620
What’s this?

00:21:18.620 --> 00:21:22.200
“Nagoya specialty Koumi sauce and
Nagoya’s famous local Kouchin chicken.

00:21:22.200 --> 00:21:25.830
The Kouchinmi yakisoba bread incorporation is a

00:21:25.830 --> 00:21:27.850
great success at the Pantasia Nagoya Branch.”

00:21:27.850 --> 00:21:30.380
Koumi sauce!

00:21:30.380 --> 00:21:31.170
Its real name...

00:21:31.170 --> 00:21:33.420
High Grade Koikuchi sauce.

00:21:33.420 --> 00:21:36.260
Just as the name indicates,
it’s a sauce with a strong taste.

00:21:36.260 --> 00:21:38.510
From this intersection, with Nagoya in the center,

00:21:38.510 --> 00:21:41.360
there’s an overwhelming response
to it in the Toukai area.

00:21:41.850 --> 00:21:44.350
Of course, liking its taste depends
on each individual person.

00:21:44.350 --> 00:21:46.360
There are people who like light taste as well.

00:21:46.360 --> 00:21:50.480
However, when it comes to yakisoba
bread, there’s another thing to keep in mind.

00:21:50.480 --> 00:21:51.370
Right, Ken?

00:21:51.370 --> 00:21:52.870
Exactly!

00:21:53.870 --> 00:21:55.870
As you know,

00:21:55.870 --> 00:22:00.370
things that are put in bread have
to be stronger-tasting than normal.

00:22:05.330 --> 00:22:08.130
Just like hamburgers, and hot dogs.

00:22:08.130 --> 00:22:10.890
And of course... yakisoba bread!

00:22:12.880 --> 00:22:16.880
Azuma, your enemy,
Spencer Henley Hokou,

00:22:16.880 --> 00:22:18.980
is Italian-trained, but he’s an American.

00:22:19.890 --> 00:22:23.980
He’s probably an expert on the
methods of making food taste strong.

00:22:24.980 --> 00:22:27.600
In other words, for this theme,

00:22:27.600 --> 00:22:30.570
he can be called the ultimate enemy!

00:22:54.480 --> 00:22:56.240
On this chest, big and strong

00:22:56.240 --> 00:22:58.360
A look that glitters and doesn't lose.

00:22:58.360 --> 00:23:00.360
That's what I searched for, fumbling in the wind.

00:23:00.360 --> 00:23:01.660
The answer for now is...

00:23:01.660 --> 00:23:04.580
For now, I'll watch the situation and wait for a chance.
I got the patience to wait at a distance.

00:23:04.580 --> 00:23:06.370
A prisoner who just screams is no good.

00:23:06.370 --> 00:23:08.160
Just Follow Me! I'll lend you my shoulder occasionally.

00:23:17.010 --> 00:23:18.260
It's by no means a fleeting dream.

00:23:18.260 --> 00:23:21.140
Let this sentiment reach you. Heart to Heart, Soul to Soul.

00:23:21.140 --> 00:23:23.180
The seasons turn. Splendid as a spring storm.

00:23:23.180 --> 00:23:24.590
Win Big is the motto.

00:23:26.270 --> 00:23:29.390
Does a thing like eternity really exist?

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:31.230
And so we... C'mon.

00:23:32.610 --> 00:23:36.780
Yeah, yeah, we live to touch the one shining moment.

00:23:53.710 --> 00:23:57.590
To all the soldiers fighting today using the tail wind...

00:24:05.490 --> 00:24:08.080
Can you really make delicious yakisoba bread?

00:24:08.080 --> 00:24:09.960
In order to win against this unknown-prefecture person,

00:24:09.960 --> 00:24:12.130
simply learning to make yakisoba isn’t enough!

00:24:12.130 --> 00:24:12.930
What?!

00:24:12.930 --> 00:24:14.710
After making us practice so much...!

00:24:14.710 --> 00:24:15.800
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan,

00:24:15.800 --> 00:24:17.020
The best possible team!!

00:24:17.020 --> 00:24:18.730
We’re going to win with Onono Komachi-san!

00:24:18.730 --> 00:24:19.890
Be sure to see it!

00:24:20.510 --> 00:24:22.640
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:23.080 --> 00:24:24.720
The Worcester sauce used in yakisoba was

00:24:24.720 --> 00:24:28.060
developed in the 19th century in
the town of Worcester, England.

00:24:28.060 --> 00:24:30.060
It’s something that was accidentally produced from

00:24:30.060 --> 00:24:31.620
the fermentation of vegetables, fruits and spices.

00:24:31.620 --> 00:24:33.860
Really?!
